\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Acute Neuropixel recordings while optogenetically stimulating serotonin release. (a) Saggital cartoon drawing of serotonergic neurons in the DRN projecting throughout the brain (green). An optical fiber is positioned directly above the DRN through the cerebellum through which the 5-HT neurons can be activated with blue light. (b) A coronal histological section of the DRN showing expression of channelrhodopsin. (c) A coronal histological section showing the fluorescent tract of a Di-I coated Neuropixel insertion. (d) Neuropixel insertion trajectories, aligned to the Allen Brain reference atlas, across all seven mice. Typically seven insertions were made per mouse, color of each insertion indicates mouse identity.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
